-- Runs checked FOO compute kernels through Vulkan.
public define device as opaque.
public define buffer as opaque.
public define kernel as opaque.

-- Availability means a Vulkan loader and compute device are present.
public use "gpu" function available giving boolean.
public use "gpu" function open giving failable pointer to device.
-- Name is owned text; release it with text.release.
public use "gpu" function name(device pointer to device) giving failable text.
public use "gpu" function capacity(device pointer to device) giving failable unsigned.
public use "gpu" function supports(device pointer to device, feature text) giving failable boolean.
public use "gpu" function reserve(device pointer to device, size unsigned) giving failable pointer to buffer.
-- Borrowed views of coherent host-visible device memory. Serialize host
-- access with dispatch and keep the buffer alive while a view is in use.
use "gpu" function mapped(buffer pointer to buffer) giving failable sequence of constant byte.
use "gpu" function mutable(buffer pointer to buffer) giving failable sequence of byte.
public function view(source pointer to buffer) giving failable sequence of constant byte borrowing source {
  give mapped(source) try.
}
public function edit(source pointer to buffer) giving failable sequence of byte borrowing source {
  give mutable(source) try.
}
-- Transfers cover the entire buffer and finish before returning.
public use "gpu" function upload(buffer pointer to buffer, source sequence of constant byte) giving failable nothing.
public use "gpu" function download(buffer pointer to buffer, destination sequence of byte) giving failable nothing.
-- Typed transfers use four bytes per decimal 32 element.
public use "gpu" function send(buffer pointer to buffer, source sequence of constant decimal 32) giving failable nothing.
public use "gpu" function receive(buffer pointer to buffer, destination sequence of decimal 32) giving failable nothing.
public use "gpu" function push(buffer pointer to buffer, source sequence of constant unsigned 32) giving failable nothing.
public use "gpu" function pull(buffer pointer to buffer, destination sequence of unsigned 32) giving failable nothing.
-- Prepare compiles a checked FOO function declared `for gpu`.
public use "gpu" function prepare(device pointer to device, entry text) giving failable pointer to kernel.
-- Available only within a `for gpu` function.
public use "gpu" function index giving unsigned.
public use "gpu" function local giving unsigned.
public use "gpu" function group giving unsigned.
public use "gpu" function lane giving unsigned.
public use "gpu" function subgroup giving unsigned.
public use "gpu" function width giving unsigned.
public use "gpu" function broadcast(value decimal 32) giving decimal 32.
public use "gpu" function barrier giving nothing.
-- Shared storage is local to one workgroup and requires explicit dispatch.
public use "gpu" function shared(size unsigned) giving sequence of decimal 32.
-- Returns the previous value; addition wraps at 32 bits.
public use "gpu" function atomic(buffer sequence of unsigned 32, index unsigned, value unsigned 32) giving unsigned 32.
public use "gpu" function bind(kernel pointer to kernel, index unsigned, buffer pointer to buffer) giving failable nothing.
-- Launch uses a one-dimensional global range; finish waits for queued work.
public use "gpu" function launch(kernel pointer to kernel, count unsigned) giving failable nothing.
-- Dispatch requires a positive local size that divides count.
public use "gpu" function dispatch(kernel pointer to kernel, count unsigned, group unsigned) giving failable nothing.
-- Plane and volume use row-major linear gpu.index values.
public use "gpu" function plane(kernel pointer to kernel, x unsigned, y unsigned, columns unsigned, rows unsigned) giving failable nothing.
public use "gpu" function volume(kernel pointer to kernel, x unsigned, y unsigned, z unsigned, columns unsigned, rows unsigned, layers unsigned) giving failable nothing.
public use "gpu" function finish(device pointer to device) giving failable nothing.
public use "gpu" function discard(kernel pointer to kernel) giving failable nothing.
public use "gpu" function dispose(buffer pointer to buffer) giving failable nothing.
public use "gpu" function close(device pointer to device) giving failable nothing.
